A||||7||86 SE||cracked front end paint||||1||
Z||000000||86 SE||10-17-2000||05:26 PM||||Has any one ever hit something with the front end of your car and had the paint crack if so do you think that putting touchup paint on it then wiping the excess off would it stay in the cracks & how do u think it would look.||||reg||1
Z||000001||fropuff||10-17-2000||05:34 PM||||I got my GT repainted this August.  I had the same problem with the cracked paint.  It was pretty bad.  I used some chemical stripper and the DA on the fascia, and it turned out pretty good, until the paint.  The cracks showed up again through the paint.  They aren't as bad as before, but you can still see them.  Turns out the entire fascia had stress cracks from a little "bump" to the fascia.  If yours is just the paint, I would strip it down first, then get it repainted.  It would turn out a lot better.  The only way to fix it if it's like mine is to get an entire new fascia.  Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||10-17-2000||06:14 PM||||Yea, if you just want to touch it up so it's not as noticable that would be ok.  I'd make sure the paint is a close match tho.  If you want a permanant fix it, I'd sand the cover down and have it repainted.  Then again, if the rest of the car is in dire need of paint, I'd do the temporary fix and start saving to have the whole car painted.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">           <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||the need for speed||10-17-2000||07:41 PM||||how much for a good paint job||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||10-17-2000||08:34 PM||||Depends on your definition of good. Complete panel off repaint, then reassembly.$3500.  Maacco repaint $700. Twenty cans of color match paint $100.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fret Naught||10-19-2000||01:23 AM||||That is the main reason I painted my front end with the pickup bed liner, I used a gun that the shop loans out, and I painted it on just like a bra. Some people don't like it, most think it was a great idea. I am very happy with it, plus it puts an end to rock chips as well<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7300004.JPG"> ||||reg||12
Z||000006||Tigger||10-19-2000||11:20 AM||||Fret, that is truly an inventive idea, a bra without the bra.  From seeing smaller pics of your car before I just assumed it was a bra.<P>I wouldn't do that to my own Fiero right now, but that would be great if the nose was chipped up really bad or even torn.  I'd fix the tear and look into that to salvage the nose because the surface wouldn't have to be perfect.<P>Cool man, nice Fiero BTW.||||reg||14
Z||000007||Fret Naught||10-20-2000||01:36 AM||||Thanks Tig,<BR>Yeah I had to make a decision, the front was chipped and cracked pretty bad, so I took the cheap and painless way out.  Fortunately for me it turned out OK||||reg||7
